<title>USA: Advantage Q2 net climbs on return on equity.</title>
<headline>Advantage Q2 net climbs on return on equity.</headline>
<dateline>KENOSHA, Wis. 1997-04-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Advantage Bancorp Inc said Thursday an increase in its return on equity helped earnings rise in the second fiscal quarter ended March 31.</p>
<p>The bank holding company said net income reached $2.5 million, or $0.73 a share, up from $2.2 million, or $0.60, in the same period last year.</p>
<p>Advantage Bancorp said its return on equity rose to 11.2 percent from 9.2 percent in the second quarter of 1996.</p>
<p>Advantage Bancorp shares closed off 1/4 Thursday at 39-1/4.</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk (312) 408-8787))</p>
